.el .ds Aq '
.TH "skillastic register" 1  "skillastic register " 
.SH NAME
skillastic register \- Create (or reuse) a .skillastic workspace for one or more projects and index them for daemon monitoring
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskillastic register\fR [\fB\-\-mandatory\fR] [\fB\-\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATHS\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create (or reuse) a .skillastic workspace for one or more projects and index them for daemon monitoring
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-mandatory\fR
Recursively scan the home directory (or /home for \-\-system) plus the roots in the user\*(Aqs global config (~/.config/skillastic/config.json), registering every project found. Opt a directory out with a .skillasticignore file in it
.TP
\fB\-\-system\fR
Index into the system\-wide registry instead of the per\-user one
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<INTERVAL>\fR [default: 300]
Poll interval for each registered daemon, in seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-depth\fR \fI<MAX_DEPTH>\fR [default: 6]
Max directory depth to scan below each root (\-\-mandatory only)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Report what would happen without writing or starting anything
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATHS\fR]
Project directories to register (defaults to the current directory). With \-\-mandatory, treated as extra scan roots
